{
  "slug": "prep-compact",
  "name": "Prep Compact",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Claude Code's auto-compact fires late and its generic summary often drops the files, decisions, and blockers you needed. The post-compact session then veers off course.\n\nprep-compact nudges you earlier: a UserPromptSubmit hook watches your transcript's byte delta since the last compact. When it crosses a configurable threshold (default 4 MB ≈ 450K tokens on Opus 4.7), Claude is prompted to invoke the prep-compact skill, which drafts a tailored /compact <mini-schema> covering goal/next/files/decisions/state.\n\nYou paste, run /compact, and the post-compact session resumes correctly. Invoke /prep-compact:prep-compact manually any time to refresh the draft before compacting.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `prep-compact` (Use when preparing to compact the conversation due to context size — typically triggered by the hook-emitted context-size…)\n- **Hooks** (2): `UserPromptSubmit`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install prep-compact@claude-community` from `koenvdheide/prep-compact`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "hook": 2
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
